 values such as 10.075 (multiplied ou\u001b[68Gto 1007.49999999\r\u001b[10C\u001b[1B99999 \u001b[18Gnd rounde\u001b[28G \u001b[30Gown). It now trims the floating-point\u001b[68Gdust\u001b[73Gbefore\u001b[80Groun\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;231mding half-up; added tests for these cases.                               \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B Thinking for \u001b[1m1s\u001b[22m, running \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m shell commands\u001b[38;5;246m · 42s\u001b[39m…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  $ git \u001b[13GC /work diff \u001b[27G-stat &&\u001b[36Gecho \"---DIFF---\" && git -C /work\u001b[70Gd\u001b[72Gff -- src tests && \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Be\u001b[8Gho \"---UNTRACKED---\"\u001b[29G&&\u001b[32Ggit\u001b[36G-C\u001b[39G/work status --short\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
